  "unreadable": [],
  "uncertain": [
    "Connector grouping: 64 pads form a two-deep ring around a 45-degree rotated square; corner 2x2 blocks are shared by two edges and were assigned clockwise (top corner to top-right edge, right corner to bottom-right, bottom corner to bottom-left, left corner to top-left). Grouping and start ends are a judgement call.",
    "Physical order: no USB connector and no pin numbers; \"top\" rule applied to diagonal edges by starting at the end that is higher in the image.",
    "Pad-to-label mapping derived from silkscreen GPIO numbers (top-left, bottom-left, top-right edges) and by tracing leader lines (bottom-right edge, where silkscreen numbers are rotated and not legible). GP46/GP47 leader lines touch; their pads were assigned from legible silkscreen 46/47.",
    "Silkscreen G under every GND pad was not individually confirmed; \"G\" added to GND functions where silk G was seen near ground pads."
  ],
  "notes": "Functions combine the printed column header with the circled instance number and signal (e.g. column SPI, circled 0, RX -> \"SPI0 RX\"). Silkscreen abbreviations (VB, 3V, 3E, RU, AV, D+, D-, SC, SD, BS) listed first in functions."
}
